tColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(33,369.2) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(33,-297.3) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>Ni is formed in excited state and comes to ground state by <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.229ex\" height=\"1.486ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -441 543 657\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FE\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FE\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-ray emission.</p>\n<p>The <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.229ex\" height=\"1.486ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -441 543 657\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FE\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FE\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-rays are high energy electromagnetic rays. These rays are generally emitted when a nuclei in